// @run
// @log 2.5
// THE LEAF THE ALLOW-LIST COULD NOT TYPE, NOW RUNNING — and the file keeps its name because a
// dozen headers and two inventories cite it as "the control for the split". What it controls is
// no longer a decline.
//
// WHAT IT PINNED. `nested-array-inferred-empty-push.vl` covers the leaves the inferred-empty
// nested-array synthesis could type: i32, boolean, a literal union, string, f64, i64. This file
// held the OUTSIDE of that set, and the answer was a loud `index receiver is not an array or
// string`, because the alternative had been shipped once and was a miscompile.
//
// WHY THE ALLOW-LIST EXISTED. The synthesis typed the row from the arena
// (`arrLitNestedElemKind`), but the annotation it writes is resolved BY NAME, so its authority
// is `refArrElemKind(<elem> + "[]")` and `rlInternName` banks the FIRST kind against a rep key.
// The two agreed on exactly the supported set. An `f32[]` leaf was kind 4 from the arena and
// kind 10 by name; a nested `i32[][]` leaf 4 and 9. Either way the outer list's backing was
// typed as the i32-list wrapper while a different wrapper was stored into it.
//
// WHY IT DOES NOT ANY MORE (D702). `arrLitNestedElemKind` IS `refArrElemKind` now, over the one
// producer (`refElemArrName`) — there is no second derivation left to disagree with, so the
// leaf set stopped being a parameter of the design. Two things had to come with it, and they
// are the two the old header named as "a real design step": the kind-9 intern goes inner-first
// through `ensureRefElemTy` so the inner wrapper lands at a strictly lower slot, and the intern
// declines any element the ref-list layer cannot NAME (`nameIsRefArray`), which is what keeps
// an unresolvable inline shape on master's loud reject instead of on a bogus row.
//
// THIS LEAF IS THE KIND-10 ONE — `f32[]`, whose element is the `$fl32TypeIdx` wrapper, and the
// `fa32Used` flag the empty-literal arm never had. It reaches the outer binding only through
// `.push`, with no declared destination anywhere in the module, so nothing else in the program
// forces that pair: the flag block is what makes it exist.
function f32Leaf() {
  const outer = []
  const inner: f32[] = [1.5, 2.5]
  outer.push(inner)
  print(outer[0][1])
}
f32Leaf()
